{
  "function": "parseBlob",
  "source": "src/main/launchers/epic/session.ts",
  "note": "decode: none\narg0 is the blob JSON as LauncherSessionStore.decrypt (src/main/services/sessions.ts) hands it to the Epic adapter: a string from the vault, not file bytes, so it is a plain value. Every Data value is a placeholder.\nRefusals: JSON.parse errors are recorded with V8's SyntaxError message exactly as Node prints it (a Rust port must map its parser errors to these texts or to the same name and message); every shape refusal is Error \"Stored Epic session has an unexpected shape\".\nNo size or depth cap in the function. JSON.parse has no nesting limit at these depths; see adv-depth-200 (serde_json stops at 128 by default).",
